{
  "version": "2.21",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "JnygO",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Activos",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "WpnvG",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Activos — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "B73zD0",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 1.4.0 · updated: 2026-10-21\n\n1. PURPOSE\nThe Activos tab: the three tiers of interest in a symbol (D9, named per D48) — Holdings (open positions), Watchlist (watchlist_items) and Tracked (the catalogue the instance syncs) — plus the two ways data gets in: the trade sheet and the CSV importer. Historial holds the three lists with no other home (D43, D60).\n\n2. ENTRY POINTS\n- Holdings / Watchlist — BottomNav tab (/assets, assets#index; ?tab=watchlist)\n- Registrar movimiento — the primary button above the tabs opens /trades/new inside a <dialog> (D11, components/_sheet_dialog); the asset detail opens it pre-filled\n- Historial, Importar movimientos, Tracked — the three foot-of-list rows under either tab (/positions, /trades/import, /tracked). All three carry HeaderBar back to /assets\n- Rows link to the asset detail in cockpit.pen\n- Buscar (D125) — the search icon in TopBar on every screen that shows TopBar (screens with a HeaderBar have none), and the field in TopBarDesktop on every desktop screen, whose results open as a dropdown. /search on mobile carries HeaderBar back to /dashboard. Activo desconocido is /market/:symbol for a symbol the catalogue lacks\n\n3. SCREENS (left → right, by band)\nHoldings\n- Holdings · Default — summary with the unrealised-gain chip, the sheet button, holdings by market value (D68), each with its share of the patrimonio and its gain\n- Holdings · Vacío — nothing open: no summary (D120), the empty state's door is the importer\n- Holdings · Sin consolidar — no FX rate: the notice replaces the summary\n- Holdings · Sin cotización — a held asset has no quote: \"Valuación no disponible\" replaces the summary, that row shows a dash, and the list falls back to alphabetical\nWatchlist\n- Watchlist · Default — rows ordered by distance to their own alert threshold, then by day move (D68)\n- Watchlist · Vacía\nRegistrar movimiento\n- Registrar movimiento · Sheet — a USD buy into a held position: projection and FX card showing\n- Registrar movimiento · Con teclado — D11's acceptance: the footer survives the keyboard (the note beside it)\n- Registrar movimiento · CETES — a fixed-income buy asks for Vencimiento; MXN hides the FX card\nHistorial\n- Historial · Default — Movimientos, Dividendos cobrados, Posiciones cerradas; the two movements within 30 days carry the edit and delete icons (MovementItem's Acciones slot), the older one has none\n- Historial · Editando — a movement replaced in place by its edit form (trades/_edit_row)\n- Historial · Confirmar borrado — a movement replaced in place by the delete confirmation (trades/_confirm_delete_row)\n- Historial · Vacío\nTracked\n- Tracked · Default — catalogue rows, the budget last on mobile\n- Tracked · Agregar activo — the typeahead and the six fields it fills (D64)\n- Tracked · Sin fuente — an asset the provider cannot name, with its fix in place (D46)\n- Tracked · Sin coincidencias — a filter that matches nothing\n- Tracked · Vacío — an empty catalogue: no budget bar, no legend\nImportar CSV\n- Importar CSV · Default, Revisión, Símbolos desconocidos (#401, D62, D63, D65)\nBuscar (D125)\n- Buscar · En tu catálogo, Catálogo y Yahoo, Fuera de tu catálogo, Sin resultados, Yahoo no responde; Activo desconocido · Default, Yahoo no responde\nDesktop\n- Holdings, Registrar movimiento (the same dialog, centred), Tracked (list beside the budget) and Buscar · En tu catálogo (the results as a dropdown under the field). The rest reflow (D4)\n\n4. BUSINESS RULES\n- The summary renders only while something is open (D120); the unrealised gain is a signed chip beside the figures, not part of the Invertido line. Without an FX rate the summary becomes the Sin consolidar notice and rows keep their own currency\n- Without a quote or a rate, holdings fall back to alphabetical order (trading/use_cases/load_assets.rb)\n- Money per D10: the summary declares the currency, rows in it drop the symbol, anything else keeps its ISO prefix. Historial's trade and dividend rows keep theirs because they mix\n- The summary is followed by a caption that dates the oldest held quote in CDMX and says where to find sources; a missing date, stale quotes and a failed sync each get their own line (shared/_valuation_caption). A missing quote removes the composite instead of valuing it at zero (shared/_valuation_notice)\n- A holding row leads with its value and follows with the day's move, a dash when there is no previous close (D69, ADR-021); a third line states its share of the patrimonio and its unrealised gain; both are absent without a consolidated total (Sin consolidar, Sin cotización). No state chip, no confluence dots (D85)\n- A watchlist row reads \"falta X%\" when an alert threshold exists, \"sigues ±X%\" from entry_price otherwise\n- The sheet asks for Vencimiento only on a fixed-income buy; the FX card hides when the currency is blank or MXN; the average-cost projection shows only on a buy into the held symbol in its own currency (trades/new.html.erb, trade_sheet_controller.js)\n- A movement executed within the last 30 days can be edited or deleted in place from Historial (trade.rb)\n- Tracked counts the whole catalogue; the filter narrows the list only. Seguir shows on the Tracked tier alone; a paused row dims, a sourceless one does not (D46)\n- The budget bar is in spend order — Holdings, Watchlist, the rest — over active stocks and ETFs only (D82); with none of those it is absent\n- An import is all-or-nothing unless the owner chooses to leave the unknown symbols out\n- Buscar (D125): the catalogue answers first, by symbol or name, from two characters, with no provider call; a hit opens the asset. Yahoo is asked only when the catalogue has no match or on Buscar «…» en Yahoo Finance; its results leave out symbols already tracked, and its failure never hides catalogue results. Rastrear tracks the symbol at once and lands on its page. Option contracts are not offered\n\n5. COPY SOURCE\nconfig/locales/es-MX.yml — assets.index, assets.tracked, trades.new, positions.index, trade_imports.*, comun.sin_tc_*, comun.cancelar, comun.guardar. Row figures: AssetsHelper. Buscar: search.results.* (en_tu_catalogo, en_yahoo, buscar_en_yahoo, rastrear, nada, yahoo_caido), market.unknown.yahoo_lo_tiene, nav.buscar, plus assets.tracked.buscar, buscar_placeholder, buscar_vacio, sin_resultados, no_encontrado, agregado and comun.tipo_activo. FX note date: FxRatesController (date_label).\n\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\n- \"Guardado. Registra el siguiente.\" above the sheet after Guardar y registrar otro\n- A refused save in the sheet (trades.errores.titulos_insuficientes, tc_faltante, a validation error) arrives as a flash alert toast (trades_controller.rb), not inside the sheet\n- /trades/new opened directly (the PWA shortcut pwa.manifest.registrar, or no JS) renders the form as a full page in the shell, not a sheet (trades/new.html.erb)\n- The importer's error line, and the other refusals (invalid_rows, missing_fx_history, repeated_external_ids, unsupported_asset_type): the same card with the detail listed below it\n- Import track_missing: the flashes \"Di de alta %{count} símbolos. Vuelve a subir tu archivo.\" and \"Di de alta %{count} de una vez. Voy por %{pending} más con el proveedor y te aviso al terminar.\" (trade_imports.track_missing.*)\n- The budget exhausted or unlimited — exhausted: the headline reads \"Sin llamadas\" and the detail \"Agotado hasta mañana\". Unlimited: the headline reads \"Sin límite\"\n- A save after editing returns the row to normal with the flash \"Movimiento actualizado.\"; a delete removes it with \"Movimiento eliminado.\"; a validation failure redirects to Historial with the error as a flash (trades.flash.*)\n- The edit window lapsing between render and click: the flash \"Sólo se pueden editar los movimientos de los últimos 30 días.\" / \"Sólo se pueden eliminar los movimientos de los últimos 30 días.\" (trades.errores.muy_antiguo_*)\n- The typeahead results are an overlay in code; the artboard draws them in flow\n- A Watchlist tab with nothing held — the summary is absent\n- Empty states and the drop zone have a dashed border — the .pen format has none\n- Buscar with an empty or one-character query: the field and nothing else\n- Buscar · Catálogo y Yahoo when Yahoo fails: the Yahoo no responde notice replaces the Yahoo section\n- Buscar when Yahoo is rate limited: the same notice as Yahoo no responde\n- After Rastrear: the asset page with \"%{symbol} se agregó a Tracked.\"\n- Activo desconocido when Yahoo does not know the symbol either: the empty state alone, no row\n\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nD125 — shipped; the kit TopBar and TopBarDesktop carry search since kit 1.3.0.\n\n8. HISTORY\n→ Log frame, below this brief. Reasoning before 2026-09-16: git show 120600bb:design/V2_REMAINING.md (ACT-*).\n",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
